# Hooks and shell scripts must keep LF wherever they are checked out. A commit-msg hook whose
# shebang line ends in CRLF is not executable on Linux, which would silently disable the guard
# for exactly the contributors who did not write it.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Gradle wrapper must keep LF wherever it is checked out. With CRLF its shebang
# line breaks on Linux, and committed from Windows without the executable bit the
# Android job fails with "./gradlew: Permission denied".
apps/android/gradlew text eol=lf

# TOOLS.md is generated by `pnpm docs:tools` and its bytes are compared against that
# generator's output by apps/server/test/tools-doc-drift.test.ts. Checked out with CRLF - which
# core.autocrlf=true does on Windows - that comparison fails on a clean clone, for a file nobody
# edited. CI runs on Linux and never sees it.
TOOLS.md text eol=lf

# The web app manifest is generated by `pnpm --filter @haelan/web manifest` and its bytes are
# compared against that generator's output by apps/web/test/manifest.test.ts, the same shape as
# TOOLS.md above and the same failure: checked out with CRLF it fails for a file nobody edited.
# Found the hard way, by a rebase re-checking the file out and turning a green branch red.
apps/web/public/manifest.webmanifest text eol=lf

# The phone glance's parser fixtures are written by apps/server/test/android-glance-fixture.test.ts
# and compared byte for byte against what the server sends, the same shape and the same failure.
apps/android/app/src/test/resources/glance/*.json text eol=lf

# The workflow files are read as text by seven test files in scripts/test, and
# android-release-workflow.test.ts anchors most of its patterns to the start and the end of a
# line. Checked out with CRLF the carriage return sits between the last character and the end of
# the line, so the end anchors miss and the match fails for a file nobody edited: the same shape
# as TOOLS.md and the manifest above, and found the same way, by a rebase re-checking the
# workflows out and turning a green branch red. Nothing reads them with CRLF on purpose - the
# runners that execute them never see one.
.github/workflows/** text eol=lf
